xsnip (2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Multi-monitor support through Xinerama: without -s the screen under the
    pointer is grabbed, after -s the screen where the selection was made; the
    new -a/--all takes the whole virtual screen.
  * The editor window is bounded by its own screen and positioned relative to
    it, so it no longer straddles two monitors.
  * New "cancel" button: close without saving.
  * Text input now shows a caret at the insertion point, sized as the font.
  * Fix: strokes jumped up by the toolbar height when the mouse was released
    (the panel offset was missing when repainting saved operations).
  * Fix: the drawing cursor was shown over the toolbar.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:10:00 +0300

xsnip (2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Screenshot of the whole screen or a mouse-selected region.
  * Minimal editor: pen and text, sizes in percent of min(width, height).
  * Five-colour palette, configurable via --colors and chosen with --color.
  * Settings (colour, sizes, tool, window type and position) persist in
    $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xsnip/config.
  * --window dialog|normal and --pos center|tl|tr|bl|br for tiling WMs.
  * Clipboard is served by a forked X11 selection owner (PNG, INCR for
    large images), so the data survives the process exit.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0300
